meta {
  name: 3. Revoke API Key
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/api-keys/1/revoke
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # Revoke API Key

  Deactivates an API key without deleting it. The key will no longer work for authentication.

  ## Security:
  - Requires JWT authentication
  - Can only revoke your own keys
  - Immediate effect - key stops working instantly

  ## Path Parameters:
  - `id`: API key ID to revoke

  ## Response:
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "API key revoked successfully"
  }
  ```

  ## Use Cases:
  - Security breach: immediately disable compromised keys
  - Temporary suspension: revoke without losing history
  - Key rotation: revoke old key before creating new one

  ## Note:
  - Revoked keys can be seen in the list with `is_active: false`
  - To permanently remove, use DELETE endpoint instead
  - Revocation is immediate and irreversible
}
